; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Rose Curves
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     rose, polar coordinates, cosine, fractions, petals
; SUMMARY:  Plots the mathematical roses r = cos(k x angle) for eight values of k and shows how k decides the number of petals.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   A rose curve is drawn by letting the distance from the center be
;   cos(k x angle). As the angle goes round, the distance swells and
;   shrinks, tracing petals. When k is a whole number, odd k gives k
;   petals and even k gives 2k petals. When k is a fraction n/d, the
;   curve takes longer to close and makes overlapping petals.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Edit the ROSES list: each entry is [n d] for k = n/d.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * polar coordinates with a changing distance
;   * negative distances: cos can be below 0, and the point flips to
;     the opposite side, which is why even k gives double petals
;   * a fraction n/d closes after d turns (or 2d turns), found with GCD
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Predict the petals for k = 6 and k = 7, then add them.
;   * Try [1 3], [5 4] and [8 5].
;   * Use SIN instead of COS. What changes?
; ============================================================

make "roses [[2 1] [3 1] [4 1] [5 1] [3 2] [7 3] [5 4] [8 5]]
make "size 80

to gcd :a :b
  if :b = 0 [output :a]
  output gcd :b remainder :a :b
end

; How many degrees until the rose with k = n/d closes up.
; With n/d in lowest terms: d turns if n x d is odd, else 2d turns.
to closeangle :n :d
  localmake "g gcd :n :d
  localmake "n :n / :g
  localmake "d :d / :g
  output ifelse 1 = remainder :n * :d 2 [180 * :d] [360 * :d]
end

to rose :n :d :cx :cy :color
  setpencolor :color
  penup
  for [a 0 closeangle :n :d 2] [
    localmake "r :size * cos :a * :n / :d
    setxy :cx + :r * sin :a :cy + :r * cos :a
    pendown
  ]
  penup setxy :cx - 20 :cy - :size - 22 setpencolor [90 90 90]
  label ifelse :d = 1 [word "|k = | :n] [(word "|k = | :n "/ :d)]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [252 250 246]
setpensize 2
setlabelheight 14
foreach :roses [
  make "col remainder # - 1 4
  make "row int (# - 1) / 4
  rose first ? last ? -300 + 200 * :col 150 - 285 * :row ~
       item # [[200 50 80] [230 120 30] [40 150 90] [50 110 210] [150 60 180] [210 70 140] [30 140 160] [120 90 60]]
]
